CON-16: book a subarea's runoff as the water that left it during the step

getSubareaRunoff() integrates the ponded depth over the step with the
nonlinear-reservoir ODE, so the depth change already contains the outflow,
but it then takes the runoff rate at the END of the step,
Alpha*(d - Ds)^5/3, and books it over the whole step. On a rising
hydrograph that overstates the outflow, on a falling one it understates it,
and the two do not cancel: the volume sent to the outlet differs from the
water that left the ponded depth. For a subarea with routing (N > 0 and
Alpha > 0), use the depth the ODE removed divided by the step instead. Every
step without outflow is unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-16_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
index 7c1d97c..cf7655f 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
@@ -956,6 +956,7 @@ double getSubareaRunoff(int j, int i, double area, double precip, double evap,
     double    surfEvap;                // evap. used for surface water (ft/sec)
     double    infil = 0.0;             // infiltration rate (ft/sec)
     double    runoff = 0.0;            // runoff rate (ft/sec)
+    double    dNoRunoff = 0.0;         // ponded depth if nothing ran off (ft)
     TSubarea* subarea;                 // pointer to subarea being analyzed
 
     // --- no runoff if no area
@@ -1000,6 +1001,7 @@ double getSubareaRunoff(int j, int i, double area, double precip, double evap,
     else
     {
         subarea->inflow -= surfEvap + infil;
+        dNoRunoff = subarea->depth + subarea->inflow * tStep;
         updatePondedDepth(subarea, &tRunoff);
     }
 
@@ -1009,6 +1011,11 @@ double getSubareaRunoff(int j, int i, double area, double precip, double evap,
     // --- compute runoff volume leaving subcatchment for mass balance purposes
     //     (fOutlet is the fraction of this subarea's runoff that goes to the
     //     subcatchment outlet as opposed to another subarea of the subcatchment)
+    //     (with routing, the runoff over the step is the depth that left the
+    //     subarea while its ponded depth was integrated, not the end-of-step
+    //     rate times the step)
+    if ( subarea->N > 0.0 && Alpha > 0.0 )
+        runoff = MAX(0.0, dNoRunoff - subarea->depth) / tStep;
     Voutflow += subarea->fOutlet * runoff * area * tStep;
     return runoff;
 }
